          "eval_mode": "substring",
          "prediction": "To determine how many albums the musician had by the time they were featured in Forbes Africa in May during the 2010s, we need to establish the timeline of their career. Since they released their first album in the 1970s and had a total of 67 albums by the time of their death at age 66, we can infer that they had a prolific career spanning several decades.\n\nAssuming they continued to release albums consistently throughout their career, it is reasonable to estimate that they had released a significant number of albums by the early 2010s. Given that they were still active in the early 2000s and participated in interviews during the 2010s, it is likely that they had released a substantial portion of their total albums by that time.\n\nTo provide a more precise estimate, we can consider that if they had 67 albums by their death, and assuming they had a steady output, they might have had around 50-60 albums by the early 2010s. \n\nThus, a concise step toward the final answer is to estimate that by the time they were featured in Forbes Africa in May during the 2010s, they likely had around 50-60 albums.",
